  "passage": "A school held a mental health day with workshops on stress, sleep, friendship, and asking for help.\nSome students joked about it at first. Others were relieved that the school was finally discussing problems they often hid.\nA counselor explained that mental health is not only about serious illness. It includes daily habits, emotions, support, and pressure.\nStudents practiced breathing exercises and learned where to seek help.\nThe day did not solve everyone's worries, but it made them easier to name.\nSilence can make problems feel private and shameful. A school that speaks openly gives students permission to care for their minds.",
